BandC wrote:
> About this "protection racket" strategy: Given the fact that some
> classes start with a good amount of gold, is this strategy sort of
> expected from them (to be able to survive later on)?

No.  IME, the protection racket is a really bad idea.  The hardest part
of the game is the early game; by the mid-game (post-Sokoban,
pre-Valley) things have gotten a lot easier and after the mid-game
you'll have pretty much the same protection whether or not you did the
racket.

So for me, the racket basically makes the hard part of the game
significantly harder and the mid-game at best slightly easier--and
that's assuming that the AC gains are worth the lower HP you'll have.

That said, the racket can be fun to try sometimes.


